{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 34, :comments ["<b>And Esau despised, etc.</b> That is, he had long despised it, and therefore Jacob took it from him. And it is found in the book of Rabbi Yehudah the Hasid: from here you learn that if a wicked person has a Torah scroll or some other mitzvah in his possession, it is permitted for a righteous person to deceive him and take it from him."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:06:03.839913631Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}